{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Pick the number that tags your declarations, and decide whether your users write it."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A kind is a 32-bit number that every record carries. A ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/documentation\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/LinkerSet","type":"reference"},{"text":" of a kind holds the records","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"declared with that kind and no others, so one program can hold your routes, another library’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"analytics events and a third’s migrations without any of them seeing the others.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Choosing-the-number","text":"Choosing the number","type":"heading","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Any number other than 0 works. 0 marks an empty slot, and the macros refuse it. The convention is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"four ASCII letters that name the thing, read as one byte each: “rout” is "},{"code":"r","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"o","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"u","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"t","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", which is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"0x72","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"0x6F","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"0x75","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"0x74","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so the kind is "},{"code":"0x726F_7574","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". The letters make it unlikely that two"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"libraries pick the same number, and they stay readable in a hex dump of the binary. Swift computes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one for you:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let kind = \"rout\".utf8.reduce(0) { $0 << 8 | UInt32($1) }  \/\/ 0x726F_7574"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Give the kind a name for the code that reads it:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["extension LinkerSetKind {","    static let routes = LinkerSetKind(rawValue: 0x726F_7574)  \/\/ \"rout\"","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A library that reads the set for its users keeps the name internal: the macro writes the kind as a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"number, so its users’ files never need it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"When-two-libraries-pick-the-same-number","text":"When two libraries pick the same number","type":"heading","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No compiler sees every module at once, so nothing can check that a kind is unique. If two libraries"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"choose the same number, their records land in the same set. A record still hands over its value"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"only when asked for its own type, so a set of a type your library owns ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Route"},{"type":"text","text":", not "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"String"},{"type":"text","text":")"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"holds only your declarations. Read your records as a type of your own, and a clash costs nothing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"but the time to skip the other library’s records."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Writing-the-kind-at-each-declaration","text":"Writing the kind at each declaration","type":"heading","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/LinkerSetEntry(kind:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" takes the kind as an integer literal. It has to be a literal because the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"macro writes it into the binary at compile time; a named constant isn’t visible to the macro:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["enum Routes {","    @LinkerSetEntry(kind: 0x726F_7574)  \/\/ \"rout\"","    static let home = Route(path: \"\/\")","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"That suits a kind used in a few places. A typo in the number puts the declaration in the wrong","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"set without any error, though.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Giving-your-users-a-macro","text":"Giving your users a macro","type":"heading","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A library that asks its users to register things gives them a macro with the kind built in, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"they write ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Route","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and never see the number. The macro lives in a small compiler plugin built on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the LinkerSetsMacroSupport module, whose documentation walks through the plugin, the macro’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"declaration and the package’s targets. The plugin can also require a protocol of every type it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"registers, so ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on a type that isn’t an event fails to compile where it’s written.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"LinkerSets"}],"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","title":"Declaring a kind"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/linkersets\/declaringakind"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/DeclaringAKind","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/FindingRecords","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/WhatTheMacrosRefuse","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/ReplacingARegistry","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/PlatformsAndLinking"],"anchor":"Guides","generated":true}],"kind":"article","references":{"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/LinkerSetEntry(kind:)":{"type":"topic","title":"LinkerSetEntry(kind:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/LinkerSetEntry(kind:)","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/linkersetentry(kind:)","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Declares a record of ","type":"text"},{"code":"kind","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" whose value is this declaration’s.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"macro","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"LinkerSetEntry","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"kind","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s6UInt32V","text":"UInt32","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}]},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/WhatTheMacrosRefuse":{"title":"What the macros refuse","type":"topic","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/WhatTheMacrosRefuse","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/whatthemacrosrefuse","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Every declaration a record can’t describe is a compile error, with a message that says why."}],"role":"article"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/ReplacingARegistry":{"kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/replacingaregistry","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/ReplacingARegistry","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Move a central list of event types, routes or registrations onto declarations that find"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"themselves."}],"title":"Replacing a hand-written registry","role":"article"},"doc://LinkerSetsRuntime/documentation/LinkerSetsRuntime/LinkerSet":{"title":"LinkerSet","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/documentation\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/LinkerSet","url":"\/documentation\/linkersetsruntime\/linkerset","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Every record of one kind, across every image the program has loaded, and the values they"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"produce."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"LinkerSet","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"LinkerSet","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/FindingRecords":{"url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/findingrecords","kind":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/FindingRecords","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Read every declaration of a kind, as the type you expect."}],"title":"Finding records","role":"article"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets":{"type":"topic","title":"LinkerSets","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Declarations that register themselves at compile time and are found at run time across every module a program links."}],"role":"collection"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/PlatformsAndLinking":{"url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/platformsandlinking","kind":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/PlatformsAndLinking","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Where records are found, how, and which test shows it."}],"title":"Platforms and linking","role":"article"}}}